I take my sturdy umbrella and step out of the house.
It is raining very heavily outside.
I reach the bus stop to go to the office.
Water has collected everywhere on the streets.
After a while, a BEST bus arrives.
I carefully board the bus.
I sit on a window seat and look outside.
The rain has completely changed Mumbai's streets.
The bus conductor comes to me.
"Madam, ticket," he says.
I give him the money and take the ticket.
I say to him, "Dada, a lot of water has collected outside, hasn't it?"
He looks out the window and says, "Yes, madam."
I say, "It rained heavily yesterday too."
"But today the water has completely flooded the roads."
The conductor smiles and moves ahead.
The bus moves forward slowly through the water.
I like this rain very much.
